From a3670fed190a11e8ac652ebc721f37e707543f00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:53:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 253/272] clk: mediatek: mt6858: Keep the bootloader's clocks
 for blocks without clocks in DT

UFS and USB take a placeholder clock in the DT, the UART only its 26 MHz
baud clock, ECCCI no clocks at all, and nothing drives the SMI common
port yet. Their real clocks therefore have no user in Linux, and
clk_disable_unused would turn off the root file system's host, USB, the
running modem's interfaces and the display's memory port.

Mark those clocks CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED until the drivers that use them
take them.
---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6858-infra_ao.c |  8 ++++
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6858-mm.c       | 23 +++++++--
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6858-peri_ao.c  | 21 ++++++---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6858-topckgen.c | 55 ++++++++++++++--------
 4 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

